cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper.
title: 'ecg-kan: one-class ECG biometric verification from wavelet modulus-maxima
  features'
abstract: One-class ECG biometric verification on the PhysioNet ECG-ID database. Each
  heartbeat is reduced to 26 values summarising wavelet transform modulus-maxima ridges
  across five frequency bands, and one detector is trained per person on that person's
  enrolment beats alone. Six detectors are compared, including a compact Kolmogorov-Arnold
  network autoencoder with learnable B-spline edges.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/usmhic/ecg-kan
keywords:
- ECG biometrics
- wavelet transform modulus maxima
- one-class classification
- Kolmogorov-Arnold networks
- anomaly detection
